/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Lambda λ is the actual air-fuel ratio divided by the stoichiometric air-fuel ratio for the fuel.
   - λ = AFRactual / AFRstoich
   - AFRactual is the actual air-fuel mass ratio; AFRstoich is the stoichiometric ratio, 14.7:1 for petrol; λ is dimensionless.
   - The ECU runs closed-loop fuel trim.
   - The sensor does not measure AFR directly.
   - The narrowband zirconia sensor is an oxygen concentration cell.
   - E = (R T / (4 F)) ln(pO2,ref / pO2,exh)
   - E is the cell voltage in volts; R = 8.314 J/(mol·K) is the gas constant; T is absolute temperature in K; F = 96485 C/mol is the Faraday constant; pO2,ref is the oxygen partial pressure in reference air; pO2,exh is the oxygen partial pressur
   - In rich exhaust the oxygen partial pressure on the exhaust side is low, so the cell produces about 0.8–0.9 V.
   - A heater inside the sensor brings it to light-off quickly.
*/
