/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Knock is the self-ignition of the unburnt end gas ahead of the flame front, after the spark.
   - q is charge (C); d is charge sensitivity (C/N); F is knock force (N); V is output voltage (V); Cf is feedback capacitance (F).
   - A MEMS accelerometer has a proof mass on silicon springs.
   - Torque sensors measure twist in a shaft.
*/
