/* book Worked example: Q: A piezoelectric knock sensor has charge sensitivity d = 2 pC/N. A knock force of 50 N acts on it. The charge amplifier has feedback capacitor Cf = 1000 pF. Find the charge produced and the output voltage.
   1. Given d = 2 pC/N = 2×10⁻¹² C/N.
   2. Given F = 50 N.
   3. q = d F = 2×10⁻¹² C/N × 50 N = 1×10⁻¹⁰ C = 100 pC.
   4. Given Cf = 1000 pF = 1000×10⁻¹² F = 1×10⁻⁹ F.
   5. V = q / Cf = 1×10⁻¹⁰ C / 1×10⁻⁹ F = 0.10 V.
   Answer: The charge is 100 pC and the charge-amplifier output is 0.10 V. */
