/* book exam traps: Do not amplify all engine noise: knock detection uses a band-pass filter around the knock frequency and a crank-angle window. | A gyroscope measures angular rate, not angle; integrating rate drifts because of bias and noise. | Piezo charge sensitivity is in pC/N (or pC/g), and the charge-amplifier output is q ÷ Cf; using the cable capacitance in place of Cf gives the wrong voltage. | LIDAR time of flight is round trip: divide c t by 2. Mixing ns and s gives a factor of 10⁹ error. | A torque sensor measures shaft torque, not engine brake torque; mounting and shaft material affect sensitivity. */
